        <p class="text-gold/85 font-bold tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-[10px] sm:text-xs mb-6"
           style="text-shadow: 0 0 6px rgba(0,0,0,1), 0 0 14px rgba(0,0,0,1);">
          V5 &middot; Countdown Pic_5 &middot; logo halo + per-line dark blobs
        </p>

        <!-- Logo with stacked drop-shadow halo: 3 layers blurring out
             progressively for a soft dark feathered glow. The seal
             itself stays crisp because drop-shadow renders the blur
             UNDER the alpha shape, not on the image pixels. -->
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-10 animate-fade-in">
          <picture>
            <source srcset="/images/logos/countdown250-seal-navy-blue.webp" type="image/webp" />
            <img
              src="/images/logos/countdown250-seal-navy-blue.png"
              alt="The Official Countdown 250 Ball — July 3, 2026 — Washington, D.C."
              class="w-[340px] sm:w-[440px] md:w-[520px] h-auto"
              style="filter: drop-shadow(0 0 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.85)) drop-shadow(0 0 48px rgba(0,0,0,0.6)) drop-shadow(0 0 96px rgba(0,0,0,0.4));"
            />
          </picture>
        </div>

        <div class="relative mb-10">
          <div class="relative z-10">

            <!-- DESKTOP arched SVG.
                 New per-line filter: feMorphology dilate radius 35
                 (much wider than letter spacing so adjacent letters'
                 halos MERGE into one continuous blob along the line)
                 + feGaussianBlur stddev 30 (soft feathered edges) +
                 feFlood black 0.7 (dark but not opaque). Net effect:
                 a soft, oval-ish dark blob behind each text line, no
                 visible boundary. -->
            <svg
              viewBox="0 -65 1000 295"
              class="hidden md:block mx-auto h-auto mb-8"
              style="width: min(1024px, calc(100vw - 2rem));"
              aria-label="Where will you be… when the clock strikes 250?"
              role="img"
            >
              <defs>
                <filter id="v5-line-blob-desk" x="-30%" y="-100%" width="160%" height="300%">
                  <feMorphology in="SourceAlpha" operator="dilate" radius="35" result="expanded"/>
                  <feGaussianBlur in="expanded" stdDeviation="30" result="blurred"/>
                  <feFlood flood-color="black" flood-opacity="0.70" result="darkfill"/>
                  <feComposite in="darkfill" in2="blurred" operator="in" result="halo"/>
                  <feMerge>
                    <feMergeNode in="halo"/>
                    <feMergeNode in="SourceGraphic"/>
                  </feMerge>
                </filter>
                <path id="v5-arch-line1-desk" d="M 50 130 Q 500 0 950 130" fill="none" />
                <path id="v5-arch-line2-desk" d="M 50 215 Q 500 85 950 215" fill="none" />
              </defs>
              <text fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.92)" font-size="30" font-weight="300" font-style="italic" font-family="'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif" filter="url(#v5-line-blob-desk)">
                <textPath href="#v5-arch-line1-desk" startOffset="50%" text-anchor="middle">Where will you be&#8230;</textPath>
              </text>
              <text fill="#ffffff" font-size="47" font-weight="400" font-style="italic" font-family="'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif" filter="url(#v5-line-blob-desk)">
                <textPath href="#v5-arch-line2-desk" startOffset="50%" text-anchor="middle">when the clock strikes 250?</textPath>
              </text>
            </svg>

            <!-- MOBILE arched SVG (same blob filter, scaled radii) -->
            <svg
              viewBox="0 -40 600 200"
              class="block md:hidden w-full max-w-md mx-auto h-auto mb-8"
              aria-hidden="true"
              role="img"
            >
              <defs>
                <filter id="v5-line-blob-mob" x="-30%" y="-100%" width="160%" height="300%">
                  <feMorphology in="SourceAlpha" operator="dilate" radius="22" result="expanded"/>
                  <feGaussianBlur in="expanded" stdDeviation="20" result="blurred"/>
                  <feFlood flood-color="black" flood-opacity="0.70" result="darkfill"/>
                  <feComposite in="darkfill" in2="blurred" operator="in" result="halo"/>
                  <feMerge>
                    <feMergeNode in="halo"/>
                    <feMergeNode in="SourceGraphic"/>
                  </feMerge>
                </filter>
                <path id="v5-arch-line1-mob" d="M 30 95 Q 300 25 570 95" fill="none" />
                <path id="v5-arch-line2-mob" d="M 30 150 Q 300 80 570 150" fill="none" />
              </defs>
              <text fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.92)" font-size="34" font-weight="300" font-style="italic" font-family="'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif" filter="url(#v5-line-blob-mob)">
                <textPath href="#v5-arch-line1-mob" startOffset="50%" text-anchor="middle">Where will you be&#8230;</textPath>
              </text>
              <text fill="#ffffff" font-size="40" font-weight="400" font-style="italic" font-family="'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif" filter="url(#v5-line-blob-mob)">
                <textPath href="#v5-arch-line2-mob" startOffset="50%" text-anchor="middle">when the clock strikes 250?</textPath>
              </text>
            </svg>

            <!-- 'The Official' + h1 left without halo per Mike's spec
                 (his list of three lines was just the two arched lines
                 + the once-in-a-lifetime closing). -->
            <p class="font-heading italic font-bold text-lg sm:text-xl md:text-2xl text-gold mb-2 tracking-wide">
              The Official
            </p>

            <h1 class="font-heading font-bold text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-[4.5rem] text-white leading-[1.05] mb-6 tracking-tight">
              Countdown 250 Ball
            </h1>

            <div class="w-20 h-px bg-gold/70 mx-auto mb-5"></div>

            <!-- 'A once-in-a-lifetime moment.' with stacked text-shadow
                 to mirror the SVG blob effect: multiple wide-blur dark
                 layers stack up to form a soft dark blob behind the
                 glyphs. The text itself stays crisp because the
                 browser renders text-shadow under the glyph alpha. -->
            <p class="font-heading italic font-light text-lg sm:text-xl md:text-2xl text-gold/95 mb-8"
               style="text-shadow: 0 0 14px rgba(0,0,0,0.95), 0 0 28px rgba(0,0,0,0.8), 0 0 56px rgba(0,0,0,0.55), 0 0 96px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
              A once-in-a-lifetime moment.
            </p>

            <div class="flex justify-center">
              <a
                href="/#tickets"
                class="bg-red hover:bg-red-light text-white px-10 py-4 text-sm font-semibold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase transition-all rounded shadow-lg hover:shadow-xl hover:-translate-y-0.5"
              >
                Compare Ticket Options
              </a>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============================================================ -->
    <!-- Color key                                                    -->
    <!-- ============================================================ -->
    <section class="bg-white py-10">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
        <div class="bg-navy/[0.02] border border-navy/20 rounded-lg p-6">
          <p class="text-navy font-semibold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-xs mb-4">Color key</p>

          <p class="text-navy font-semibold text-sm mb-2">Top hero on this page (DEBUG view) &mdash; three distinct backgrounds</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-navy/85 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-5">
            <li class="flex items-start"><span class="inline-block w-5 h-5 rounded-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5 mr-3" style="background: rgba(40,120,255,0.55); border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.15);"></span><span><strong class="text-navy">Bright blue</strong> &mdash; the FULL-HERO photo overlay. Covers the entire hero behind everything else (this is what the perceived &lsquo;darker outer ring&rsquo; was on live &mdash; the photo overlay sitting outside the dome). On the live site this same layer is black at 0.55 opacity.</span></li>
            <li class="flex items-start"><span class="inline-block w-5 h-5 rounded-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5 mr-3" style="background: rgba(255,102,0,0.90);"></span><span><strong class="text-navy">Bright orange</strong> &mdash; the feathered ball/dome SVG ellipse. Sits in the middle of the hero, on top of the blue layer. On the live site this is dark grey at 0.70 opacity.</span></li>
            <li class="flex items-start"><span class="inline-block w-5 h-5 rounded-sm flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5 mr-3" style="background: rgba(255,235,0,0.85); border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.15);"></span><span><strong class="text-navy">Bright yellow</strong> &mdash; the per-letter halos behind each glyph in the two arched lines. They merge into one blob per text line. On the live site this is black, sized to each letter.</span></li>
          </ul>

          <p class="text-navy font-semibold text-sm mb-2">V2 (middle hero)</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-navy/85 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-5">
            <li><strong class="text-navy">Photo:</strong> &lsquo;Countdown Pic_1&rsquo; from Downloads, optimized + saved as <code class="text-navy/80 bg-white/50 px-1 rounded">/images/event/hero-countdown-pic-1.jpg</code> (1600&times;900, ~349 KB).</li>
            <li>NO full-hero overlay, NO dome, NO per-letter halos. Pure photo + crisp text + button.</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="text-navy font-semibold text-sm mb-2">V3</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-navy/85 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-5">
            <li><strong class="text-navy">Photo:</strong> &lsquo;Countdown Pic_2&rsquo; from Downloads, optimized + saved as <code class="text-navy/80 bg-white/50 px-1 rounded">/images/event/hero-countdown-pic-2.jpg</code> (1600&times;900, ~318 KB).</li>
            <li>Same setup as V2: NO overlays, NO halos. Pure photo + crisp text + button.</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="text-navy font-semibold text-sm mb-2">V4</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-navy/85 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-5">
            <li><strong class="text-navy">Photo:</strong> &lsquo;Countdown Pic_3&rsquo; from Downloads, optimized + saved as <code class="text-navy/80 bg-white/50 px-1 rounded">/images/event/hero-countdown-pic-3.jpg</code> (1600&times;900, ~344 KB).</li>
            <li>Same setup: NO overlays, NO halos.</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="text-navy font-semibold text-sm mb-2">V5 (bottom hero) &mdash; targeted feathered backgrounds</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-navy/85 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-5">
            <li><strong class="text-navy">Photo:</strong> &lsquo;Countdown Pic_5&rsquo; (1600&times;900, ~296 KB).</li>
            <li>NO full-hero overlay, NO dome.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-navy">Logo:</strong> stacked drop-shadow halo (24 px / 48 px / 96 px blur radii at decreasing opacity) so the seal sits on a soft dark glow.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-navy">Three text lines</strong> (&lsquo;Where will you be…&rsquo;, &lsquo;when the clock strikes 250?&rsquo;, &lsquo;A once-in-a-lifetime moment.&rsquo;) each get a dark feathered blob behind the line. Implemented via SVG filter (dilate 35 + blur 30 + black 0.7) on the arched lines, and stacked text-shadow on the once-in-a-lifetime line.</li>
            <li>&lsquo;The Official&rsquo; and &lsquo;Countdown 250 Ball&rsquo; are NOT in the list of three lines so they stay plain (no halo).</li>
          </ul>

          <p class="text-xs text-navy/70 leading-relaxed pt-2 border-t border-navy/10">
            Pure photo + text test on all four new pics (V2&ndash;V5). Tells us which one reads best with zero darkening, and which (if any) is the right candidate to swap onto the live home page.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
